preConditionHook:
// THE BAR REACHES DOWN TO THE RECENT FLOOR. Long: the low of the bar `lag`
// bars ago comes to within tolAtr ATRs of the lowest low of the levelLookback
// bars ENDING ONE BAR BEFORE IT -- Grimes's resting bid at the base's support.
// Mirrored: the high reaches up to the window's highest high, his offer at
// resistance.
//
// SIDES EXCHANGED FROM TouchOfRecentExtreme, which is the momentum read: ITS
// long side is the bar's highest price reaching the window top (the magnet
// above), where this one's long side is the bar's lowest price reaching the
// window floor (the bid at support). A side exchange is NOT the per-placement negate toggle -- the
// DistanceAboveRecentLow / PullbackFromRecentHigh precedent -- so neither rule
// can be placed to do the other's job. Not SwingPointTestHolds, which needs a
// CONFIRMED pivot and also requires the low NOT to break it; not
// NearMissLevelReversal, a two-sided band plus a close-up term; not
// PullbackFromRecentHigh, which measures the low DOWN FROM the window top.
//
// THERE IS DELIBERATELY NO CAP on how far through the level the bar trades: a
// resting limit order fills on the way down, so the test is ONE-SIDED with a
// tolerance band above the level, never a two-sided band.
//
// THE WINDOW EXCLUDES THE TESTED BAR, so the bar cannot set the level it is
// tested against; the EL twin hands Lowest/Highest the SHIFTED price series
// (the low series offset by lag + 1) rather than lagging the function's own
// result -- the StopBeyondRecentRangeExtreme / TouchOfRecentExtreme spelling.
//
// THE TOLERANCE IS AN ATR FRACTION (merge decision 7), where
// TouchOfRecentExtreme's is in ticks: the ATR form is the corpus's settled
// level tolerance and is what makes the same 0.25 mean the same thing on @ES
// and on @HO. That is the deliberate reconciliation, not an oversight.
//
// `lag` follows StrongTrendBar's convention: it exists so that "touched one
// bar ago, and is now well away from the level" is TWO placements rather than
// a composite rule. At lag 0 this is the merged key LowTouchesRecentLow term
// for term (its baseLookback 10 / touchTolAtr 0.25 / atrLookback 14 are a grid
// point of this rule), which is why that key is not a second file.
//
// MultiWalk's WFSafe_AvgTrueRange is a ROLLING accumulator, not a fresh mean:
// AtrProfitTarget's block verbatim, including the TWO separate accumulator
// statements and the re-seed when the length changes.
//
// The window loops mirror EasyLanguage's Extremes(): seeded at the window's
// first bar, scanning the rest, strict comparison under the EL relational
// tolerance -- hence el_gt / el_lt, as in Breakout.
//
// Deepest bar touched: max(lag + levelLookback, atrLength + 1).
if (atrLenState != (int)atrLength) {
    atrSum = 0.0;
    for (int aa = 0; aa < (int)atrLength; ++aa) {
        hiV = high[aa] > close[aa + 1] ? high[aa] : close[aa + 1];
        loV = low[aa] < close[aa + 1] ? low[aa] : close[aa + 1];
        atrSum += hiV - loV;
    }
    atrLenState = (int)atrLength;
} else {
    outIdx = (int)atrLength;
    hiV = high[0] > close[1] ? high[0] : close[1];
    loV = low[0] < close[1] ? low[0] : close[1];
    hiO = high[outIdx] > close[outIdx + 1] ? high[outIdx] : close[outIdx + 1];
    loO = low[outIdx] < close[outIdx + 1] ? low[outIdx] : close[outIdx + 1];
    atrSum += hiV - loV;
    atrSum -= hiO - loO;
}
atrValue = atrSum / (int)atrLength;
levelLow = low[lag + 1];
levelHigh = high[lag + 1];
for (int i = 1; i < (int)levelLookback; ++i) {
    if (el_lt(low[(int)lag + 1 + i], levelLow)) levelLow = low[(int)lag + 1 + i];
    if (el_gt(high[(int)lag + 1 + i], levelHigh)) levelHigh = high[(int)lag + 1 + i];
}
